a b s t r a c t
Stiff person syndrome (SPS) is a rare autoimmune neurological disorder with antibodies
against antigens involved in neurotransmission of gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA). About
10% of patients with SPS may develop ataxia. This cerebellar variant is a distinct subset of
SPS with more severe and complex clinical phenotype.
We report the clinical, neuropsychological and neuroradiological ﬁndings in a 39-year-
old female with cerebellar variant of SPS.
